# NOTICE

## Third-party code adapted in this repository

`tools/baseline.mjs`, `tools/imagediff.mjs` and `tools/profile.mjs` are adapted
from the capture/diff/profile harness in:

    mshumer/Claude-of-Duty — https://github.com/mshumer/Claude-of-Duty
    Copyright (c) 2026 mshumer
    Licensed under the MIT License

Two ideas in that harness are load-bearing here and were taken directly:

1. **Per-shot page isolation.** Reusing one browser page across shots leaks
   particle age, accumulation buffers and auto-exposure state forward, so
   repeated runs of the same capture set diverge. Isolating each shot in a
   fresh page is what makes the comparison bit-reproducible, and therefore what
   makes a per-pixel diff usable as a gate at all.

2. **Hitch attribution via per-frame WebGL program counts.** A median frame
   time hides exactly the stalls that make an interactive scene feel broken. A
   jump in `renderer.info.programs.length` on the same frame as a spike
   identifies the spike as a shader-compilation stall.

The upstream MIT license text is reproduced above and applies to those portions.

## What differs here

The upstream harness was retrofitted onto a finished project, which required a
separate remediation pass to remove wall-clock dependencies before the pixel
gate could pass. This repository inverts that order: the determinism contract in
`ARCHITECTURE.md` is a precondition on all code, and the gate was proven green
against a stub scene before any content existed. See `METHODOLOGY.md`.
